<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
	<!--
		Keeps dragonium out of the hands of vanilla traders without hiding it from
		vanilla's own systems.

		Dragonium sits in the ResourcesRaw category, like plasteel, steel, uranium
		and gold, so it appears beside them in the storage filters and is treated
		as a raw resource everywhere else. Three vanilla trader kinds stock raw
		resources with a StockGenerator_Category on that category -
		Base_Outlander_Standard, Base_Neolithic_Standard and Orbital_BulkGoods -
		and StockGenerator_Category takes ANY def inside the category whose
		tradeability lets a trader sell it, with no tech gate unless the generator
		asks for one (the field defaults to Archotech, i.e. no limit). Left alone,
		the metal would turn up in outlander and orbital stock as well as
		Dragonia's, which is the whole reason this patch exists.

		The fix is vanilla's own: each of those generators already carries an
		excludedThingDefs list, used to keep Bioferrite and the Odyssey panels out
		of them. This adds PMM_Dragonium to all three lists. One xpath covers every
		matching generator in the game, and the conditional around it means a
		renamed or removed generator leaves a quiet log rather than an error.

		Note this only covers vanilla. Another mod's trader is free to roll
		ResourcesRaw and could still stock dragonium; the two explicit lines on
		Dragonia's trader kinds (Defs/TraderKindDefs/TraderKinds_Dragonia.xml)
		remain the only intended source.

		The dragon orbs (2026-09-22) are the same problem in a different category.
		PMM_DragonOrb and PMM_DragonOrbDecor sit in BuildingsFurniture, so they can
		never be BUILT (they carry no designationCategory and no costList) - but
		furniture is exactly what vanilla traders do stock: three vanilla kinds roll
		BuildingsFurniture with a StockGenerator_Category, and one of them is the
		orbital trader. So the orbs are excluded from all three by name as well.
		Unlike the ResourcesRaw generators, none of those three carries an
		excludedThingDefs list today, so the operation below has an else-branch:
		append to a list another mod made, otherwise add the whole element.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/li[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][categoryDef="ResourcesRaw"]/excludedThingDefs</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<success>Always</success>
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<success>Always</success>
					<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/li[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][categoryDef="ResourcesRaw"]/excludedThingDefs</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>PMM_Dragonium</li>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</match>
	</Operation>

	<!-- Dragon orbs: the three generators that roll BuildingsFurniture. -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<success>Always</success>
		<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/li[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][categoryDef="BuildingsFurniture"]/excludedThingDefs</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<success>Always</success>
			<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/li[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][categoryDef="BuildingsFurniture"]/excludedThingDefs</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>PMM_DragonOrb</li>
				<li>PMM_DragonOrbDecor</li>
			</value>
		</match>
		<nomatch Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<success>Always</success>
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<success>Always</success>
					<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/li[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][categoryDef="BuildingsFurniture"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<excludedThingDefs>
							<li>PMM_DragonOrb</li>
							<li>PMM_DragonOrbDecor</li>
						</excludedThingDefs>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</nomatch>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
